  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 32893e18c8b32e442b8f84ac4913d667, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NpcInteractable
  interactionPoint: {fileID: 0}
  highlightObject: {fileID: 0}
  spriteRenderer: {fileID: 4571458385659737367}
  highlightTint: {r: 0.81886786, g: 0.81886786, b: 0.81886786, a: 1}
  npcName: Benlyn
  sprite: {fileID: 4723107735738678597, guid: a94fe6f45fa75874a9002f3a393c9e9f, type: 3}
  lines:
  - Hey there, traveller. We don't get many visitors around these parts. Why not sit for a moment? You look like you've walked a long way in the dark. The name's Benlyn. I've been wandering these caves for years. I think. You won't see much down here. The light left these caves long ago. But sound... sound remembers everything.
  - Why not give it a go? To send out an echo pulse, press Q on keyboard, the Y button on Xbox, or the triangle button on PlayStation. Watch how the world shows itself where your echos land. Each pulse needs a moment to gather itself, and longer if something is hunting you as that'll rattle your head a bit.
  - Platforms, walls, ledges. It all shows for a moment and then fades. Make sure to remember what you see. And if something gets too close, you've still got a blade. To use it, a mouse click will do, or the X button on Xbox and the square button on PlayStation. Keep swinging and your strikes will chain together.
  - That's all a lost explorer like me has to give. Go on, traveller. Listen to the sounds this place has to offer and your questions will be answered.
  npcCamera: {fileID: 6344331569869082}
  talkingMaterial: {fileID: 2100000, guid: 9dfc825aed78fcd4ba02077103263b40, type: 2}
